{# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   BUILD ICON — the corner link through to a product's composition in Build.

   Params:
     tile   the tile this icon belongs to (must have a live buildLink)
     row    the row, for row.buildIcon
     label  accessible label, distinct from the primary link's

   A SIBLING anchor to the primary tile link, never nested inside it: nested <a>
   elements are invalid HTML and browsers restructure them unpredictably. Stacking
   is handled in CSS (.gallery-tile__build sits above .gallery-tile__link), so a
   click on the icon reaches Build and a click anywhere else reaches the product.

   Default is an inline SVG rather than a bitmap, so it inherits colour from the
   theme and stays crisp. row.buildIcon replaces it globally when set in Craft.

   The glyph is a sliders mark — the horizontal-lines-with-dots form familiar from
   filter and settings UI — which reads as "adjust this" without the commerce
   connotation of a cart.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
<a
 class="gallery-tile__build"
 href="{{ tile.buildLink.url }}"
 rel="noopener noreferrer"
 aria-label="{{ label }}"
>
 {% if row.buildIcon is not null %}
  <img src="{{ row.buildIcon.url }}" alt="" width="20" height="20">
 {% else %}
  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75"
   stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
   <line x1="3" y1="7" x2="21" y2="7" />
   <line x1="3" y1="12" x2="21" y2="12" />
   <line x1="3" y1="17" x2="21" y2="17" />
   <circle cx="9" cy="7" r="2.25" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
   <circle cx="15" cy="12" r="2.25" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
   <circle cx="7.5" cy="17" r="2.25" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" />
  </svg>
 {% endif %}
</a>
